INV-rozob. Reproduced in THREE LINES of Python on the shipped CLI:

    """@generated"""

    from datetime import date

The import edge's src read `python:<external>:0-0:file:external_symbol` -- no
path, span 0-0. A reader has no file to open, so the edge can be neither
confirmed nor refuted, and a taint flow seeded from one names no place: 19 of
104 adjudicated flows in docs/measurements/0001, every one labelled
UNADJUDICABLE by two independent readers. It was also a MANY-TO-ONE bucket,
because make_file_id puts the literal "file" in the name slot -- so every such
file in a language shared one id and nobody could tell which imported what.

THE CHAIN: is_likely_minified heuristic 3 matches (Generated by|@generated|DO
NOT EDIT) in the first five lines with NO comment anchor, so a docstring trips
it -> tier 4 (DERIVED) -> cli.py's tier filter drops the Symbol while
DELIBERATELY KEEPING its edges (WI-pozur / ADR-0043 C2) -> ir._dedupe_key
discarded the path for the now-dangling kind="file" src.

THAT LAST STEP IS THE DEFECT, AND ITS OWN DOCSTRING GAVE THE REASON: the path
slot is "a per-reference filesystem path with no semantic identity". It IS the
identity -- it names the file that did the importing, and it is the only thing a
reader can open. The key now keeps it.

